L0262: Mutable borrow of immutable storage

The call requests exclusive write permission for a place that is not mutable. A shared reference does not acquire mutation permission merely because the referent has mutable fields. Declare a mutable owner or pass an already authorized mutable reference.

Example from `tests/corpus/reject/borrow_immutable.lc`; the full file is a regression test.

```locus
// A `&mut` argument is rooted at a binding the call may assign: a
// `let mut`, a `mut` parameter, or a `&mut` parameter. Rust refuses the
// rest with E0596, and so does Locus.
fn bump(counter: &mut u8) -> () {
    counter = counter.wrapping_add(1);
}

fn immutable_local(n: u8) -> u8 {
    let count = n;
    bump(&mut count);
    count
}

fn immutable_parameter(n: u8) -> u8 {
    bump(&mut n);
    n
}

fn behind_a_shared_reference(n: &u8) -> u8 {
    bump(&mut n);
    n
}
```

Language, as built: [1.13:1](../../atlas.html#/doc/language/spec-1.13:1).
